board:0012 unit heading INTEGRATOR width base-loss (FUN_1000_a395).  a395 turns a mobile unit's current
heading [0x26] toward its target heading [0x30], one clamped step (<=0xb6) per tick.  asm @ 0x1a395 is
WORD throughout (mov ax,WORD[di+0x30]; sub ax,WORD[di+0x26]; cwd/xor/sub abs; add WORD[di+0x26],ax; second
mode adds a clamped [0x89] slew to [0x26]/[0x30] and subtracts from [0x89]/[0x8b]).  Ghidra typed
[0x26]/[0x30]/[0x89]/[0x8b]/[0x5d] as 32-bit *(int*)/*(uint*): the 32-bit error read [0x30]-[0x26] pulled
in adjacent fields and the abs used (int)x>>0xf (a 15-bit shift on a 32-bit int) -> the heading error was
garbage and never converged (observed: [0x26] oscillated +-30000 instead of settling at the target), so a
mobile unit could not steer to a commanded heading.  Fix: rebase every field to 16-bit *(short*), matching
the WORD asm; the abs/clamp/sign-restore kept faithful.  (Sibling to 421 a1d6/a174 + 422 a401 servo -- the
same mobile-unit steering cluster.)
--- a/fist.c
+++ b/fist.c
@@ -64185,41 +64185,47 @@
