+   * cwd/xor/sub = 16-bit abs; clamp step to 0xb6; add WORD[di+0x26],ax.  Ghidra typed [0x26]/[0x30]/
+   * [0x89]/[0x8b]/[0x5d] as *(int*)/*(uint*) (32-bit) -> the 32-bit heading-error read pulled in
+   * neighbours and the abs shift (>>0xf on a 32-bit int) was wrong -> heading never converged (oscillated
+   * +-30000) and the tank could not turn to a target heading.  Rebase all to 16-bit *(short*). */
   if ((((*(byte *)(param_1 + 0x19) & 6) != 0) || ((*(byte *)(param_1 + 0x19) & 0x10) != 0)) ||
-     (*(int *)(param_1 + 0x5d) == 0)) {
